Subject: iOS: a GoldenEye ROM hack's conversion lives in Caches, as GE Plus's does

Upstream v3.14.0 converts a GoldenEye ROM hack it knows (Goldfinger 64) into
a folder of its own name in the first writable of $E/mods and $H/mods - on
iOS both are Documents (patch 0009). That is the game's own output, made
again from the player's file in added-content/ in a few seconds, so it goes
where overlay 0043 already sends GE Plus's arenas: $C/mods (Caches/mods)
first. modListRefresh() already mounts $C/mods on iOS (0043), and the "done
once per source" test (variantConvertedFrom) walks the same list, so a purged
Caches converts again behind the same notice at the next start. A conversion
an earlier build left in Documents/mods is still found and used where it is.

The patch (or zip) form's unpack goes to cache/romhacks/ through
fsChooseOutputDir("cache"), which patch 0009 already sends to Caches.

And the stamp names its source from $E. A conversion is "done once per
source": CONVERT.txt says "Converted from <realpath of the file>" and a later
start converts again when no stamp names the file it finds. On iOS the app's
data container moves on every install and update (a new UUID in the path,
Documents carried over), so every update made the hack's ~4 s, ~1 GB
conversion run again. variantCanonical() now names a file under Documents
as "$E/added-content/<name>" on iOS; the shell's settings row (PDXbla) reads
the stamp the same way. A stamp an earlier build wrote converts once more.

Every other platform is unchanged.

diff --git a/port/src/gexplusrom.c b/port/src/gexplusrom.c
index a922b5e29..91649df0d 100644
--- a/port/src/gexplusrom.c
+++ b/port/src/gexplusrom.c
@@ -716,7 +716,15 @@ static void variantReady(const char *name)
 	}
 }
 
+#ifdef PLATFORM_IOS
+// $C (Caches) first, as GE Plus's own arenas (iOS port overlay 0043): a hack's
+// conversion is the game's own output, made again from the player's file in
+// added-content/ if the system purges it. One an earlier build left in
+// Documents/mods is still found and used where it is.
+static const char *const g_VariantContainers[] = { "$C/mods", "$E/mods", "$H/mods" };
+#else
 static const char *const g_VariantContainers[] = { "$E/mods", "$H/mods" };
+#endif
 
 // the second line of a conversion's CONVERT.txt: the file it was made from
 static s32 variantStampFrom(const char *dir, char *from, u32 fromlen)
@@ -1015,6 +1023,23 @@ static void variantCanonical(const char *path, char *out, u32 outlen)
 	char *full = realpath(fsFullPath(path), NULL);
 
 	if (full) {
+#ifdef PLATFORM_IOS
+		// The app's container moves on every install and update (a new UUID
+		// in the path, Documents carried over), so a stamp naming the file by
+		// its absolute path would be stale after each one and the hack
+		// converted again. Under Documents it is named from $E instead.
+		char *home = realpath(fsFullPath("$E"), NULL);
+		const size_t homelen = home ? strlen(home) : 0;
+
+		if (home && !strncmp(full, home, homelen) && full[homelen] == '/') {
+			snprintf(out, outlen, "$E%s", full + homelen);
+			free(home);
+			free(full);
+			return;
+		}
+
+		free(home);
+#endif
 		snprintf(out, outlen, "%s", full);
 		free(full);
 		return;
